  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- Version 9.0.19\n\t\t- Literal INSERT and UPDATE values now go through the property's value converter, so a converted property (such as a DateTimeOffset stored as a string) no longer fails with an InvalidCastException.\n\n\t\t- Version 9.0.18\n\t\t- Prevention of too much optimized boolean expressions since 9.0.16 caused expressions like '(a = b) = true' to be left this way, but OpenEdge doesn't support that. This is now optimized to 'a = b' as it was before 9.0.16 while still keeping 'WHERE table.booleanfield = true' unoptimized.\n\n\t\t- Version 9.0.17\n\t\t- Fixed positional parameters, they are now always added even if they have the same name.\n        - Fixed boolean expressions where a comparison with a parameter was made, 'WHERE boolean_field <> parameter' was inadvertedly turned into 'WHERE boolean_field = 1 <> parameter'\n\t\t\n\t\t- Version 9.0.16\n\t\t- Custom OpenEdgeSqlNullabilityProcessor that prevents boolean expressions from getting optimized too much. OpenEdge demands explicit comparison with true/false, so 'WHERE table.booleanfield = true' must not be optimized to 'WHERE table.booleanfield' because that will yield a SQL syntax error.\n\t\t\n\t\t- Version 9.0.15\n\t\t- Updated EF Core to 9.0.22\n\t\t- Multi-targeting: added .Net 10\n\n\t\t- Version 9.0.14\n\t\t- Fixed boolean expressions in SELECT clause which must be wrapped in a CASE statement and then typecasted to BIT\n\n\t\t- Version 9.0.13\n\t\t- Fixed bug in previous version where 'WHERE boolean_field <> 1' was inadvertedly turned into 'WHERE boolean_field = 1 <> 1'\n\n\t\t- Version 9.0.12\n\t\t- Fixed unsupported 'WHERE boolean_field' / 'WHERE NOT(boolean_field)' by converting it back to 'WHERE boolean_field = 1' / 'WHERE boolean_field = 0'\n\n\t\t- Version 9.0.11\n\t\t- Fix ROW_NUMBER() by emulating it with a subselect\n\n\t\t- Version 9.0.10\n\t\t- Fix SELECT EXISTS expressions\n\n\t\t- Version 9.0.9\n\t\t- More fixes for boolean type, which is sql type BIT in OpenEdge\n\n\t\t- Version 9.0.8\n\t\t- Fixed support for datetime-tz\n\t\t- Fixed support for boolean type, which is sql type BIT in OpenEdge\n\n\t\t- Version 9.0.7\n\t\t- Extended support for datetimezone type\n\t\t- Fixed inline fetch/offset statements being cached incorrectly\n\n\t\t- Version 9.0.6\n\t\t- Fixed issue with boolean comparison not being translated correctly in some cases\n\t\t- Added support for DateOnly type in queries\n\n\t\t- Version 9.0.5\n\t\t- Added support for DateOnly type. This ensures that OpenEdge DATE columns are mapped to DateOnly type in EF Core.\n\n\t\t- Version 9.0.4\n\t\t- Fixed issue with OFFSET/FETCH parameters not being inlined correctly in complex queries\n\t\t- Added support for nested queries with Skip/Take",
